& [AuthorityInventory] distinguishes source, migration input, canonical authority, and implementation
  + [current_source] is preserved_unprocessed
  + [primal_identity] is strong_candidate_without_canonical_authority
  + [attention_foundation] is signed authority requiring faculties to compile as libraries rather than primitives
  + [faculty_formation] is signed migration input whose meanings remain useful but whose syntax is not runtime authority
  + [faculty_runtime] is signed architecture with implementation parked until faculty semantics are recompiled
  + [truth_frame] is signed bounded implementation authority for the existing core acceptance sequence
  + [semantic_core] is signed but limited to its existing acceptance fixtures
  + [implementation_reality] is partial and does not yet contain typed Planner, Weaver, Scribe, or Refiner participation

& [ImplementationObservation] is direct
  + [SemanticTransition] already carries before state, history review, instruction, judgments, after state, effects, faults, and proof trace
  + [ecosystem_runtime] already binds an Observer participant and performs Honesty and Security review checks
  + [missing_machine_surface] is an inspectable faculty plan, activation, return, omission reason, ledger, stage ordering, and Observer disposition
  + [missing_runtime_surface] is causally effective Planner, Weaver, Scribe, and Refiner execution under the same transition waist
  + [reuse_decision] is extend the existing transition architecture rather than create a competing faculty engine

& [DelineationResult] resolves the important collisions
  + [primal_form] is conservation, bounded transformation, and proof-bearing reinscription expressed through Cantor's transition waist
  + [faculty_program] is a compiled higher-order SAIL library and is not a language primitive
  + [constitutional_faculty] is a faculty whose participation or justified omission must be visible in every governed cycle
  + [faculty_provider] is deterministic code, one inline model pass, an isolated job, a remote model, or a human under the same return contract
  + [inscription] is a typed durable record whose authority state remains explicit
  + [candidate_inscription] does not become accepted state merely because Scribe recorded it
  + [effect] remains proposed and externally uncommitted until EffectBroker authorization
  - never: equate a faculty name with a base SAIL opcode
  - never: equate recorded material with validated or authorized material

& [PrimalCompatibilityResolution] prevents circularity
  + Cantor's minimal transition has Scribe-like conservation and Refiner-like bounded transformation obligations
  + the compiled Scribe and Refiner faculties are programs over SAIL primitives that inspect and strengthen those obligations
  + the kernel does not depend on faculty names to parse or execute base primitives
  + the faculty programs do not grant themselves authority or effect capability

& [FacultyTopology] is cyclic and governed
  + Observer binds subject, purpose, authority, consequence, current state, and unresolved frontier
  + Scribe anchors the exact before-state and later inscribes the admitted disposition with lineage
  + Weaver composes compatible bounded meanings and exposes seams, contradictions, and decomposition needs
  + Planner orders the smallest admissible path with prerequisites, dependencies, checkpoints, and stop conditions
  + Weaver and Planner cross-review until relational shape and temporal path are mutually supportable or explicitly blocked
  + Refiner minimizes the next formed delta without inventing meaning or laundering novelty
  + Honesty validates claims, support, attribution, counterevidence, and uncertainty
  + Security validates authority, boundary, reversibility, disclosure, effect, and risk
  + Observer admits, revises, reroutes, decomposes, blocks, or escalates
  + Scribe records the resulting state, proof, residual, and continuation anchor

& [ActivationResolution] preserves both integration and bounded cost
  + every cycle accounts for all seven faculties as activated or explicitly omitted
  + Observer, Honesty, Security, Scribe, and Refiner are required for every non-trivial semantic transition
  + Planner and Weaver are required for semantic mutation and effect proposal cycles
  + a pure preservation cycle may omit Planner or Weaver only with a reason accepted by Observer
  + omission is inspectable policy output rather than silent absence
  + a deterministic no_gain or not_applicable return is preferable to ceremonial model invocation

& [InputAuditRequirementSet] is CIFP-001 through CIFP-017
  + [CIFP-001] compile all faculties as typed SAIL libraries rather than primitive keywords
  + [CIFP-002] make all faculty participation or omission inspectable in every governed cycle
  + [CIFP-003] keep Observer active for subject continuity, routing, reconciliation, and disposition
  + [CIFP-004] anchor exact before-state and inscribe admitted after-state through Scribe with lineage
  + [CIFP-005] compose bounded compatible relations through Weaver while preserving seams
  + [CIFP-006] order the smallest admissible path through Planner with prerequisites and verification
  + [CIFP-007] require Planner and Weaver cross-review for composite or multi-step transitions
  + [CIFP-008] require Refiner to minimize formed deltas without semantic novelty
  + [CIFP-009] apply non-waivable Honesty and Security gates before Observer admission
  + [CIFP-010] classify inscription authority so recording never implies acceptance
  + [CIFP-011] return a typed ledger, objections, uncertainty, and unavailable context from every activation
  + [CIFP-012] preserve causally effective disagreement and answer every material objection
  + [CIFP-013] represent Observer disposition as admit, revise, reroute, decompose, block, or escalate
  + [CIFP-014] retain SemanticTransition as the single proof-bearing runtime waist
  + [CIFP-015] keep effects proposed until an authorized EffectBroker commits them
  + [CIFP-016] support deterministic, inline, isolated, independent-provider, and hybrid faculty implementations
  + [CIFP-017] prove machine validation, deterministic replay, and semantic equivalence before runtime integration

& [AuditDecision] is proceed to bounded SJS formation
  + [stable_core] is a governed cyclic faculty process around one proof-bearing SemanticTransition waist
  + [first_implementation_slice] is immutable faculty cycle machine forms plus pure structural validation and tests
  + [deferred] is provider execution, prompt projection, remote deliberation, transition integration, persistence migration, and exterior effects
  + [canonical_authority] is absent_until_signed_specification
  + [implementation_authority] is absent_until_signed_specification
